# Claude Dashboard - Environment Variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything works with ZERO config out of the box.
# The dashboard reads ~/.claude/ directly. No database, no account needed.
# Only uncomment what you need.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- Port ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: 3003 (npm run dev / setup / prod)
# PORT=3003

# -- Network binding ----------------------------------------------------------
# Host the server binds to. Default: 127.0.0.1 (localhost only - safe default).
# Set to 0.0.0.0 to expose on your LAN (e.g. to open the dashboard on an iPad).
# Only do this on a network you trust: read routes are open by design. The
# `npm run dev:lan` / `npm run start:lan` scripts set this to 0.0.0.0 for you.
# DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0

# -- Multi-Machine (optional, off by default) ---------------------------------
# Run the dashboard on several machines (laptop, Mac mini, Pi, VPS) and switch
# between them from one UI. Off by default - with nothing set, the dashboard is
# single-machine. List peer dashboards as host:port. Cross-machine data is read
# through a same-origin proxy; there is no remote command execution.
# MACHINES=mac-mini.local:3003,raspberrypi.local:3003
# LOCAL_MACHINE_ID=my-laptop
# Optional shared SQLite path for the machines registry. Default: unset (uses env).
# MACHINES_DB_PATH=/path/to/shared-machines.db

# -- RAG + Local Vector Search (optional, off by default) ---------------------
# Semantic memory search over your Claude Code history. It builds a local SQLite
# index and downloads a small on-device embedding model on first use - no
# external service and no API key required. Off by default to keep the dashboard
# zero-setup. Set to 1 to show the RAG and Context tabs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAG_ENABLED=1
#
# Vector (semantic) search additionally needs the on-device embedding model,
# which is an optional dependency kept out of the default install (its native
# deps are heavy). Enable it with: npm install @huggingface/transformers
#
# Where the RAG SQLite index lives. Default: data/rag.db (relative to cwd)
# RAG_DB_PATH=data/rag.db
#
# Directory containing your projects, used for RAG ingestion. Default: ~/Sites
# RAG_PROJECTS_DIR=~/Sites
#
# Colon-separated Obsidian vault paths to also ingest. Default: none.
# OBSIDIAN_VAULTS=~/Sites/notes:~/Documents/Obsidian Vault

# -- AI-assisted extras (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Enables RAG preference extraction, insights, compile, and semantic rerank.
# Without it those features quietly no-op (plain FTS + vector search still work).
# Setting it sends memory/session text to api.anthropic.com.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# -- Eval (optional) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Models used by the RAG eval harness (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
# EVAL_ANSWER_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# Local embedding model for eval vector search. Default: Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
# EVAL_EMBED_MODEL=Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
# Max characters of wiki corpus used per eval run. Default: 60000
# EVAL_WIKI_MAX_CHARS=60000

# -- Database (optional) ------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite for session history. Auto-created if missing.
# SQLITE_PATH=~/.claude/dashboard.db

# -- Paths / misc -------------------------------------------------------------
# WebSocket server bind host. Set to 0 for 127.0.0.1-only; anything else (or
# unset) binds 0.0.0.0. Default: 0.0.0.0
# WS_LAN=0
# Machine label used by the WS server. Default: auto-detected hostname
# MACHINE=my-machine
# Path to the tailscale binary for LAN discovery. Default: falls back to
# /usr/local/bin/tailscale, then the Tailscale.app bundle path
# TAILSCALE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/tailscale
# Base URL the standalone rag-memory MCP server (mcp-server.ts) proxies to.
# Default: http://localhost:<PORT> (PORT above, else 3003)
# CLAUDE_DASHBOARD_URL=http://localhost:3003
# Local-apps monitor integration (optional). Port + base URL of a companion
# local-apps monitor the dashboard can read from. Defaults: 9876 / localhost.
# LOCAL_APPS_PORT=9876
# LOCAL_APPS_URL=http://localhost:9876
